curtsy (0.3.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * Refactor the configuration module registry: the comptime module type
    list is now the single ordering source and drives generated ModuleRef
    entries with descriptor pointers and conf slot indexes.
  * Synchronize release metadata across the CLI version string, build.zig
    package version, man page, and changelog.
  * Make UDP sockmap acceleration conservative and adaptive: auto starts
    on the userspace batched relay and only attempts sockmap after stable
    runtime evidence (no loopback upstream, sustained large-datagram
    workload over several windows), with hysteresis/cooldown and a safe
    userspace fallback; loopback and small-packet workloads stay in
    userspace. Sustained eligible traffic may enable sockmap after five
    qualifying windows; enabled remains a best-effort forced attempt with no
    ordering guarantees. TCP auto is unchanged.
  * Close the enabled-to-auto reload race: a reload that disallows UDP
    sockmap synchronously blocks new associations from entering sockmap
    while the async teardown command is pending, and an unchanged eligible
    auto reload (e.g. a tuning-daemon limits tick) preserves the loaded
    adaptive runtime and policy instead of tearing acceleration down.
  * Make hot reload transactional: every fallible change for every rule
    (new rules, upstream generations, listeners for added protocols,
    listen backlog preflight) is staged before any matched rule is
    committed. Prepared listeners bind in a paused state and do not accept
    TCP or forward UDP until the non-failing commit activates them, so a
    failed reload leaves the whole previous configuration serving, keeps
    listeners/pools/cycle ownership on the old state, and releases the
    rejected candidate cycle normally.
  * Make loaded configurations self-contained: scalar strings are copied
    into the cycle arena so file-loaded configs stay valid after the file
    bytes are released.
  * Add a dedicated privileged `zig build test-ebpf` entry point that
    runs the real eBPF integration suite and fails loudly without
    CAP_BPF/CAP_NET_ADMIN, while the default `zig build test` stays
    unprivileged and clean.
  * Packaging: emit a real ELF build id, drop the now-useless
    libpthread.so.0 NEEDED (glibc >= 2.34 resolves those symbols from
    libc.so.6), and document the intentional static libbpf/libelf/libz/
    libzstd embedding with a Lintian override.

 -- Curtsy contributors <maintainers@example.invalid>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

curtsy (0.3.1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Cut data-plane syscall overhead across the TCP/UDP relays:
    - TCP: cached timer deadlines with throttled sweeps, 1024-event epoll
      batches, batched budget release, connection freelist, and one less
      epoll_ctl per closed connection.
    - UDP: 50ms-throttled expiry sweeps, idle-time-scheduled sockmap
      session checks (99% fewer bpf() calls under steer-heavy load),
      per-wake timestamp reuse, pointer-based association access, faster
      SocketAddr hashing, pre-sized session maps, rate-limited drop logs,
      and a cooldown after sockmap pairing failures.
    - Logging now emits one write syscall per line; the tuning daemon
      loads its kprobe observer only when a limit is auto-tuned.
  * Add performance.udpDatagramBufferBytes to size the batched UDP
    receive slots (576..65536, default 65536).
  * Build for the architecture baseline CPU by default; pass
    -Dcpu=native for host-optimized binaries.

 -- Curtsy contributors <maintainers@example.invalid>  Fri, 31 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +0000

